$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.6. Typical Esterification Procedure. Weighed
amounts of acid 2, alcohol 3, and TSIL were added to a flask with a
reflex condenser. The esterification reaction was typically allowed to
proceed for 1.5-3 h with vigorous stirring and heating at the desired
temperature. After the reaction, the system became biphasic. The upper
phase contained the expected ester 4 and was isolated by decantation.
Table 3, entry 9, yield 91.9%
