$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.5. Synthesis of SO3H-Functional Brønsted
Acidic TSILs. Equal molar of trialkanylammonium-propane sulfonate (TAAPS)
and acid solutions were mixed and stirred for 24 h at 40-80 °C. Then, the
combined solution was dried in a vacuum at 100 °C to remove the water.
The produced TSILs were washed repeatedly with diethyl ether to remove
unreacted material and dried in a vacuum again. The TSILs were analyzed
by IR, 1H NMR, 13C NMR, and MS spectroscopies, and the spectral data
agreed with their structures. 2.6. Typical Esterification Procedure.
Weighed amounts of acid 2, alcohol 3, and TSIL were added to a flask with
a reflex condenser. The esterification reaction was typically allowed to
proceed for 1.5-3 h with vigorous stirring and heating at the desired
temperature. After the reaction, the system became biphasic. The upper
phase contained the expected ester 4 and was isolated by decantation.
Table 3, entry 3, yield 85%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 1.3 molar ratio acetic acid:benzyl alcohol
