$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6.3. General Procedure for the Mitsunobu Esterification Under
Argon-Atmosphere a Schlenck-flask was charged with 1 mmol of carboxylic
acid 5, 7, 10 or 13, respectively, and 1 mmol of PPh3. Afterwards dry THF
and 1 mmol of the corresponding alcohol 2a-e were added. To this solution
1 equivalent of DTBAD was added in small portions. The progress of the
reaction was followed by TLC. After completion of the reaction the
solvent was removed and the target compound was isolated via
flash-chromatography with ethylacetate/cyclohexane as mobile phase and
silica gel as stationary phase.
4-({[(2R)-1-Ethoxy-1-oxopropan-2-yl]oxygcarbonyl)phenyl
4-(4-propylcyclohexyl)benzoate 14a, n=2. δ H (300MHz; CDCl3) = 8.12 (m,
4H; 7-H, 12-H), 7.30 (m, 4H; 6-H, 11-H), 5.31 (q, J=7.0 Hz, 1H; 15-H),
4.23 (q, J=7.1Hz, 2H; 17-H), 2.55 (m, 1H; 4-H), 1.89 (m, 4H), 1.34 (m,
18H). δ C (75MHz; CDCl3)=170.3 (C16), 164.8 (C14), 164.2 (C9), 154.6
(C10), 154.1 (C5), 131.0 (C7/C12), 130.0 (C7/C12), 126.8 (C6), 126.6
(C8/C13), 126.2 (C8/C13), 121.4 (C11), 68.8 (C15), 61.0 (C17), 44.4 (C4),
39.2, 36.5, 33.6 (2C), 32.9 (2C), 19.6, 16.7, 13.9, 13.7. HR-MS (EI, 70
eV); m/z: 466.236 (calc. 466.2355). EA: Found: C, 72.077; H, 7.3424.
C28H34O6 calculated C, 72.08; H, 7.35%.
