$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Benzyl 3-((4-methoxyphenyl)thio)-2-methyl-3-oxopropanoate (1a’) A mixture
of methyl malonic acid (4.5 g, 37.5 mmol) and benzylalcohol (2.1 g, 15
mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was cooled to 0 °C and EDC hydrochloride
(5.75 g, 30 mmol) was added in small portions. The resulting mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred for 30 min. The reaction
mixture was washed with H2O (20 mL) and extracted with aq. sat. NaHCO3 (4
× 12 mL). The combined aqueous phases were acidified to pH 3 by adding
aq. HCl (4%) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic
phases were dried over NaSO4, which was then filtered and concentrated in
vacuo. To the crude material (2.05 g, 9.8 mmol) and 4-methoxythiophenol
(2.80 g, 19.7 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (25 mL) at 0 °C was added EDC
hydrochloride (3.80 g, 19.7 mmol) in small portions and the resulting
mixture was stirred for 1 hour at room temperature. The reaction was
washed with water (20 mL), extracted with CH2Cl2 and the combined organic
phases were concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was purified by
flash column chromatography (n-hexane/EtOAc). Benzyl
3-((4-methoxyphenyl)thio)-2-methyl-3-oxopropanoate 1b as colorless oil
(2.0 g, 40%). δH (300 MHz, CDCl3): 7.43-7.37 (m, 5 H, ArH), 7.36-7.27 (m,
2 H, ArH), 7.01-6.92 (m, 2 H, ArH), 5.25 (s, 2 H, ArCH2), 3.86 (s, 3 H,
OCH3), 3.85-3-76 (m, 1 H, CH), 1.55 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3 H, CH3); δc (101
MHz, CDCl3): 194.6 (C), 169.1 (C), 160.9 (C), 136.2 (CH), 135.4 (C),
128.6 (CH), 128.4 (CH), 128.2 (CH), 117.5 (C), 115.0 (CH), 67.3 (CH2),
55.4 (CH3), 53.5 (CH), 14.2 (CH3); HRMS (ESI): calculated for C18H19O4S
[M+H]+ 331.0999, found 331.0997; υmax(neat)/cm-1: 3033, 2940, 1738, 1696,
1591, 1573, 1493, 1376;
